(
    title: "# Release evidence",
    produced_by: [
        "Produced by `cargo xtask ci --profile release`. No registry action was",
        "performed: no publish, no tag, no release, no credential use. The gate",
        "is offline and verifies only the archive it just built; reading the",
        "registry is a separate command, `cargo xtask verify-package`.",
    ],
    source_heading: "## Source",
    worktree_clean: "- Worktree: clean, including untracked files",
    candidate_version_suffix: "(both product crates, inherited from `[workspace.package]`; `ph-veml7700-als-conformance` pins the `0.0.0` sentinel and is never published)",
    deny_pass_suffix: "advisory, source, and licence policy pass",
    archive_heading: "## Prepublication archive",
    archive_intro: [
        "This is the archive Cargo builds from the tree above. It is **not** the",
        "byte-identical artifact a later `cargo publish` uploads: publishing",
        "repackages from the source tree, so the published bytes depend on the",
        "publishing machine's checkout line endings and Cargo version as well as",
        "on the commit. Publish only from this same unchanged clean pinned tree.",
        "What ties the published archive to this record is not its checksum but",
        "the commit: run `cargo xtask verify-package --version <version>` against",
        "the registry copy.",
    ],
    inventory_heading: "### File inventory and per-entry digests",
    inventory_intro: [
        "Read from the `.crate` archive, not from the unpacked directory: the",
        "unpacked copy accumulates `target/` output once its tests run.",
        "",
        "SHA-256 of each entry as packaged. These bytes are a property of the",
        "machine that packaged them, so do not compare this table across",
        "platforms; the commit-anchored table below is the one that travels.",
    ],
    verify_heading: "## Archive matches the reviewed commit",
    verify_intro: [
        "Every packaged source entry was re-derived from the Git blob at the",
        "commit the archive declares. Git normalizes line endings on the way in,",
        "so a blob is the same on every platform and this comparison does not",
        "depend on where the archive was built.",
        "",
        "A difference confined to carriage returns before newlines is a checkout",
        "artifact, reported as end-of-line-only, and passes. Any difference that",
        "survives normalization is edited content and fails. The three",
        "Cargo-generated entries exist in no commit, so they are asserted against",
        "instead: the declared commit and clean-tree flag, the dependency and",
        "feature surface of the normalized manifest against the commit's own",
        "manifests, and the packaged lock against the commit's lock.",
        "",
        "The archive naming a commit is its own claim. What makes it evidence is",
        "that every source entry then verifies against that same commit.",
    ],
    commit_inventory_heading: "### Per-entry digests against the commit",
    commit_inventory_intro: [
        "Columns: SHA-256 of the packaged bytes, SHA-256 of those bytes with",
        "line endings normalized, and the Git object id at the release commit.",
        "",
        "Two records produced from one commit on different platforms agree",
        "exactly on the second and third columns and may disagree on the first.",
        "Compare releases on the second and third. A squash merge, a different",
        "platform, or a different Cargo version all move the first column and",
        "the archive checksum without any content changing.",
    ],
    manifest_heading: "### Normalized manifest",
    vcs_heading: "### VCS metadata",
    missing_vcs: "{ \"error\": \"no .cargo_vcs_info.json in the archive\" }",
    test_boundary_heading: "## Test boundary",
    test_boundary: [
        "Two different things were tested, and the distinction matters:",
        "",
        "- **Standalone package tests** ran against the unpacked archive above.",
        "  They establish that the published crate builds and passes its own tests",
        "  in isolation.",
        "- **Driver-versus-model conformance** ran only in the repository.",
        "  `tests/device_model.rs` and the path-only `ph-veml7700-als-model`",
        "  dev-dependency are excluded from the package on purpose, so the archive",
        "  cannot rerun them. Model conformance is repository-level evidence and",
        "  must never be cited as package-level evidence.",
        "",
        "`ph-veml7700-als-model` is repository-only and unpublished.",
    ],
    not_established_heading: "## Not established",
    not_established: [
        "This evidence covers artifact identity and the implemented host boundary.",
        "It establishes no physical-device, electrical, optical, or calibrated",
        "behavior, and it is not a decision to publish.",
    ],
)
